 "applies_to": "Carrier AquaForce 30XA 140-352 air-cooled screw chillers with Touch Pilot controls and the factory BACnet/Modbus translator.",
 "summary": "On the 30XA with Touch Pilot controls, BACnet MS/TP comes from Carrier's BACnet/Modbus translator, which maps a fixed set of CCN points to BACnet objects AV_000 onward, BV_000 onward and two time schedules. The list is short (72 objects): control type, start/stop and occupancy commands, setpoints, capacity, current, demand limit and per-circuit refrigerant temperatures and pressures.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "notes": [
  "Object instances come from the translator column (AV_000 = AV 0, BV_000 = BV 0, TS_000 = schedule 0).",
  "Object names here are the CCN point names the translator maps; the live object names may differ.",
  "The same appendix lists Modbus registers 0x4000 onward for the same points."
 ],
