 "integration": {
  "summary": "Put the chiller in Network (CCN) control from the Start/Stop machine-mode selection with the Enable/Off/Remote switch closed, then command BV 0 start/stop and BV 1 occupancy through the translator. Read control type, capacity, leaving/entering fluid temperatures, and write setpoints AV 50 onward and demand limit AV 10.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 0",
    "name": "CHIL_S_S",
    "why": "Network start/stop command"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 1",
    "name": "CHIL_OCC",
    "why": "Network occupied command"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 3",
    "name": "EMSTOP",
    "why": "Emergency stop"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 50",
    "name": "csp1",
    "why": "Cooling setpoint 1"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 10",
    "name": "DEM_LIM",
    "why": "Active demand limit (writable)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 0",
    "name": "CTRL_TYP",
    "why": "Control type: Local, Network or Remote"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 4",
    "name": "CAP_T",
    "why": "Percent total capacity"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 12",
    "name": "COOL_LWT",
    "why": "Cooler leaving fluid temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 11",
    "name": "COOL_EWT",
    "why": "Cooler entering fluid temperature"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Select Network under Select Machine Mode (Start/Stop button). The control type reads CCN when the Enable/Off/Remote contact input is closed; the network then drives CHIL_S_S. For dual-chiller setups the slave must use CCN control.",
  "heartbeat": "The manual says that on loss of communication with the network, the machine starts and is controlled locally.",
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "Appendix D lists the BACnet MS/TP objects of the Carrier BACnet/Modbus translator; the Touch Pilot BACnet parameters table is marked 'Not Supported' in this manual.",
   "The translator only exposes the 72 points in its fixed map."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "In Local Off (Start/Stop button off) network commands are ignored.",
   "Plan chilled-water plant behaviour for comm loss: the unit reverts to local control and may start."
  ]
 },
 "page": "https://easybacnet.com/bacnet-points-lists/carrier/aquaforce-30xa-translator",
 "note": "Re-typed from the manufacturer's public documentation (see source). Point availability varies by firmware and options; verify against the live device."
